implementationPlan.description:
Regression check, run once and fresh from the repo root (Git Bash on Windows): `bash -c 'cfg=$(mktemp -d) && CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR="$cfg" claude plugin test scripts/mods/moe-account-switch && node --test scripts/tests/prompt-cache-launcher.test.mjs; rc=$?; rm -rf "$cfg"; exit $rc'`. It must exit 0, with every plugin test passing (the 26 existing plus the new END_SESSION tests) and the launcher suite green. The launcher suite pins that headless and --no-loop seats never load the mod: the wrapper half of the -p guarantee. This command's fresh output is the moe.complete_task verification evidence. A dry run at plan time on the current tree exited 0 (26/26, 19/19).

Then run a mutation proof on a scratch copy OUTSIDE the repo. Copy scripts/mods/moe-account-switch into a mktemp dir and run claude plugin test on the copy with its own empty mktemp CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR. Apply each mutation alone, confirm the suite fails, restore, then discard the copy:
M1 drop the workerId match;
M2 drop the action === 'END_SESSION' check;
M3 drop the surfaces check;
M4 drop the isError guard in replyOf;
M5 let END_SESSION overwrite a pending account switch (= in place of ??=);
M6 require MOE_ACCOUNT_ID for END_SESSION again;
M7 use the account toast for END_SESSION;
M8 always use the account fallback toast in exit();
M9 detect END_SESSION anywhere in the reply text (text.includes).
Record each mutation's failing test names in the step note. Use no real claude session, login or usage probe: only the plugin harness.
